<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis Bonaparte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1778">1778</a>–<a href="/years/1846">1846</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis Bonaparte was a younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, who made him king of Holland in 1806. Louis learned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, moved the court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> and tried to protect Dutch interests, which brought him into conflict with his brother. He abdicated in 1810, and Holland was annexed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-bonaparte.jpg" alt="Louis Bonaparte" width="320" height="488" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Howard Hodges · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LouisBonaparte_Holland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Herman Willem Daendels, appointed governor-general by <b>Louis Bonaparte</b>’s Kingdom of Holland, arrived in 1808, centralised the administration of Java, curbed the Javanese courts and built the Great Post Road along the north coast with forced labour.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Napoleon, wanting firmer control, turned the republic into the Kingdom of Holland in 1806 under his brother <b>Louis Bonaparte</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/batavian-republic">Batavian Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1806 Napoleon replaced the Batavian Republic with a kingdom and installed his brother <b>Louis Bonaparte</b> as king.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-holland">Kingdom of Holland</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Ajaccio, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livorno">Livorno</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.93,8.74&amp;year=1822" aria-label="Ajaccio on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4762 671 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Louis Bonaparte"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5212 941h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5212 941h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.93,8.74&amp;year=1822">What was here in 1822? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
